AndreaGuarracino/htscodecs, tag v1.6.7-kz3: samtools/htscodecs release
v1.6.7 (see version.h) plus three commits on branch karyozip.
Fork:     https://github.com/AndreaGuarracino/htscodecs
Upstream: https://github.com/samtools/htscodecs

The three commits:
  23abfe3 tok3 decoder: each name's token array comes from 1 MB chunks
          freed together, not a malloc and a realloc a name (short-read
          smooth and decode, 2M names: C instructions -10.5% and -11.6%).
  09631c6 rANS_static4x16pr.c includes <asm/hwcap.h> in the aarch64
          branch, so HWCAP_* is defined on older glibc. Dead on x86.
  2d05c60 the tok3 encoder takes its token arrays from the same chunks
          (short-read encode, 1.2M rows: C instructions -1.7%).

Only the files karyozip's Makefile compiles, and the headers they reach,
are kept. Deleted from the tree: fqzcomp_qual, rANS_static, rANS_byte.h,
htscodecs.c/.h, permute.h, varint2.h, tokchunk, and the AVX2, AVX512,
NEON and SSE4 rANS variants, which rANS_static32x16pr.c never references
under this config.h. Every kept file is byte-identical to the fork's tag;
config.h and version.h are generated by its build rather than shipped.

Resync: rebase branch karyozip of the fork onto a new upstream tag, tag
it, and copy the same subset from that tag; fix everything else in
karyozip.c.
